From: YanIanZ <iwayanbagusaryadarma@student.telkomuniversity.ac.id>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 02:13:57 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] SourbyCraft - fail loudly when work is queued on the
 undrained server queue

MinecraftServer.processQueue is only polled inside a block region threading never runs, so anything added to it (Spigot /restart, Bukkit conversations, sync chat and pre-login events) silently never executed. The field is now dev.iyanz.sourbycraft.guards.UndrainedQueue: add/offer throw an owned UnsupportedOperationException naming the caller and log it at ERROR once per caller; reads report an empty queue.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/MinecraftServer.java b/net/minecraft/server/MinecraftServer.java
index 65a83fd0a0b765106e64744de0370290ae64eebd..bfc3088469ec4b7e7863d55d38ce49a04430ed2f 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/MinecraftServer.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/MinecraftServer.java
@@ -540,6 +540,7 @@ public abstract class MinecraftServer extends ReentrantBlockableEventLoop<TickTa
     ) {
         super("Server", propagatesCrashes);
         SERVER = this; // Paper - better singleton
+        this.processQueue = dev.iyanz.sourbycraft.guards.UndrainedQueue.create(); // SourbyCraft - nothing drains this under region threading: adding fails loudly
         this.registries = worldStem.registries();
         if (false && !this.registries.compositeAccess().lookupOrThrow(Registries.LEVEL_STEM).containsKey(LevelStem.OVERWORLD)) { // CraftBukkit - initialised later
             throw new IllegalStateException("Missing Overworld dimension data");
